{"id": "EUVD-2026-93333", "enisaUuid": "2b086e35-598d-38d7-975d-b94d1f4e6c58", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: libipw: reject too-short association responses\n\nlibipw_handle_assoc_resp() reads the capability, status and aid fields\nof the 30-byte association response prefix and then computes the\ninformation element length as\n\n\tstats->len - sizeof(*frame)\n\nstats->len is a u16 and sizeof() has type size_t, so the subtraction is\nevaluated as size_t and wraps instead of going negative.  Truncating\nthat to the u16 length parameter of libipw_parse_info_param() turns a\nframe shorter than the fixed fields into a length near 64 KiB, and the\nparser then reads past the receive buffer.\n\nBoth the ipw2100 and ipw2200 management receive paths reach this\nfunction having established only that the frame carries the generic\n24-byte three-address header.\n\nReject the frame before any fixed field is touched.\n\nFound by an AI-assisted review of length arithmetic in management frame\nparsers.  Verified with a KUnit case under Generic KASAN on arm64 under\nQEMU; I do not have the hardware, so it is not tested on a real device.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:59", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/766268b429ae26d8ca599031fa962b0fe4673120", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d70bdb84cf1782039384c1ffa7a18b0303c286a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/400b89217058fac672134a0d4092c8493dadb8ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46aa75291056b6dc5faaf956dffdb3e9662477b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3025ecdb2057f866c09e059fc1466e81d6f243e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/14cb425ba1f3a5d849e3bbc3d02d84e0ae195dbb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af1b69be19c34e28c0ae54bee954b58cd076969a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/adb7118b7d2cfd7e8213c17d7d2829f353017754"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98348", "GHSA-jch8-34rh-p8cm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0788f676-aad5-36bd-886b-37e35748a705", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9e8571affd1c54b9638b4ff9844e47aae07310f6 <adb7118b7d2cfd7e8213c17d7d2829f353017754"}, {"id": "08c8517b-9f51-3cf7-b441-621baac669e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "274e925d-71d1-33e5-abe8-eec3c873cd3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9e8571affd1c54b9638b4ff9844e47aae07310f6 <d70bdb84cf1782039384c1ffa7a18b0303c286a7"}, {"id": "3e86296d-fc4b-3f4a-a4ca-dbfddc1005ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9e8571affd1c54b9638b4ff9844e47aae07310f6 <e3025ecdb2057f866c09e059fc1466e81d6f243e"}, {"id": "4461fb48-4d6d-3020-9eae-4d4981c532b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9e8571affd1c54b9638b4ff9844e47aae07310f6 <af1b69be19c34e28c0ae54bee954b58cd076969a"}, {"id": "50899591-ad52-3957-a68b-fa26c5cb503b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "60ceab85-2b6b-32dd-854f-82f99d9fb962", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9e8571affd1c54b9638b4ff9844e47aae07310f6 <46aa75291056b6dc5faaf956dffdb3e9662477b0"}, {"id": "8179bebb-1f80-3b0a-817f-9c0337afce3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "84f2b95b-6048-3e6e-b933-cdeba04a5387", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a4c0bb55-dd18-3896-a403-11c4de55acce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9e8571affd1c54b9638b4ff9844e47aae07310f6 <766268b429ae26d8ca599031fa962b0fe4673120"}, {"id": "a59beb95-5dea-3ac9-a1e9-24